Gradle uses the build setting in IntelliJ itself.
IntelliJ IDEA > Settings > Build, Execution, and Deployment > Build Tools > Gradle > Gradle JVM

If that is invalid, then and only then it will fall back to the JAVA_HOME environment variable.
This environment variable can, but should not be, hard coded in the .zshrc file.

Instead:
export JAVA_HOME=$(/usr/libexec/java_home)
export PATH=$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH

This will set JAVA_HOME to whatever the HIGHEST INSTALLED VERSION of the JDK is.

To set to a specific version, make it like so in .zshrc:
export JAVA_HOME=$(/usr/libexec/java_home -v 17)
export PATH=$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH


Note that we use a version flag so that /usr/libexec/java_home returns the version we want.
We do NOT hard code a path.